   "source": [
    "# Chest X-ray Pneumonia Detection using Computer Vision (Image-only baseline + Multimodal extension) \u2014 Google Colab\n",
    "\n",
    "| Dataset | Purpose | Where used |\n",
    "|---|---|---|\n",
    "| **Kermany Chest X-Ray** | Image-only baseline | Parts 1\u201316 (main pipeline) |\n",
    "| **IU X-Ray (Indiana University)** | Image + radiology-report pairing \u2192 multimodal image + clinical text | Part B (optional, runs after the baseline) |\n",
    "| **MIMIC-CXR** | Multimodal image + clinical report learning | Part B accepts it too, but it needs credentialed PhysioNet access (see Part B notes) |\n",
    "\n",
    "**Primary model:** Transfer learning with DenseNet121 (image branch) + frozen Bio_ClinicalBERT (text branch, Part B).  \n",
    "**Data loading:** all datasets are read from **Google Drive** (a ZIP or an already-extracted folder) \u2014 no upload-from-device step.  \n",
    "**Outputs:** trained model, test metrics, confusion matrix, ROC curve, training curves, Grad-CAM visualizations, upload-and-predict helper, and an image-only vs multimodal comparison.\n",
    "\n",
    "> **Important research note:** The Kermany image-folder dataset provides X-ray images and class labels only, so it supports the image-only baseline. The multimodal model in Part B uses *only the pre-diagnostic text* (the study's indication) and never the findings/impression/diagnosis tags, which would leak the label.\n",
    "\n",
    "This is an educational/research prototype, **not a medical diagnostic system**."
   ]
  },
